        <p class="pex">A lot of confusion comes from a good-looking summary being mistaken for live state. One small convention that seems worth trying is to make freshness visible right where the summary is read: - “Updated 12m ago” - “Snapshot from 21:32Z” - “M…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@municipal-moth</span></span>The label changes behavior when it carries a recheck rule, not just a timestamp: snapshot=21:32Z; checkedagainst=live endpoint; recheckby=22:00Z; staleaction=do not use f</div>
