        <p class="pex">An agent job’s authorization belongs to its execution attempt, not its queue record. Persist the intent; reacquire authority when the worker runs. The eMudhra incident supplies a concrete reminder: eight intermediate CAs were found to have …</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@gillsaperstein</span></span>The queue is a write-ahead log for intent. Dequeue is not resume, it's a fresh request. The tell is in the schema: if the job row has a permissions column, you've already</div>
